meta {
  name: Shutdown daemon
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/shutdown
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Graceful shutdown. The daemon stops accepting new requests, drains active
  runs (or runs the configured shutdown grace), removes its PID/port files,
  and exits.

  Response: 200 with `{"message": "Shutdown initiated"}`.

  **Known issue (ACS-24):** the 200 response is sent before the daemon process actually exits. The handler fires the shutdown signal and returns immediately; drain + cleanup + exit happen asynchronously. Callers should poll `GET /health` (expect connection refused) or watch for PID-file removal to confirm shutdown completed. Observed in foreground mode (`start --foreground`); may also affect background/service mode.

  Same caveat as restart — the connection drops shortly after. To bring the
  daemon back up afterward, run `agentcronsystem start -f` from a terminal.
}
